    "created_at": "2021-09-15T01:42:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-15T18:17:08Z",
    "body": "@underyx Thanks for the repro docker! \r\n\r\nIn your case, it looks like the `zinit ice` command which affects the starship init is somehow unsetting pipestatus as a cleanup action. I'm not sure how, since I looked through the zinit codebase and couldn't find anywhere where pipestatus is used outside of tests and the installer, but after playing around with that line and some print statements in the ZSH init, I'm pretty sure that's what's happening.\r\n\r\nI fixed it by changing the last line of `/root/.zinit/plugins/starship---starship/starship/init.zsh` to this:\r\n\r\n```\r\nPROMPT='$(/path/to/starship prompt --keymap=\"$KEYMAP\" --status=\"${STARSHIP_CMD_STATUS}\" --pipestatus \"${STARSHIP_PIPE_STATUS[@]}\" --cmd-duration=\"$STARSHIP_DURATION\" --jobs=\"$STARSHIP_JOBS_COUNT\")'\r\n```\r\n\r\ndouble-quoting the argument so that it doesn't get lost when passing args to starship, and replacing `/path/to/starship` with whatever path was there before.\r\n\r\nCould you (and anyone else affected by this) try this to see if it fixes things for you?\r\n\r\n* * *\r\n\r\nFor anyone who's calling `eval $(starship init zsh)`, you can test this fix by doing the following:\r\n\r\n1. Run `starship init zsh --print-full-init > ~/.starship.init.tmp` (or redirect to your file of choice)\r\n2. Replace the last line of `~/.starship.init.tmp` with the line above\r\n3. Replace `eval $(starship init zsh)` with `source ~/.starship.init.tmp` in your `~/.zshrc`\r\n\r\nIf this works, you can keep this as a temporary fix until the next release of starship happens.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
